# Node.js Development Workflow

## TDD Loop
- Write a failing Jest test first, then implement the code to make it green, then refactor.
- Never write implementation code without a failing test driving it.

## Type Safety Gate
- `tsc --noEmit` must pass before every commit. Zero `any` types except at explicit boundaries.
- Use `unknown` plus type narrowing instead of `any`. If `any` is unavoidable, document why.

## CI Gate
All four steps must pass in order:
1. `npm run lint` — ESLint must report zero errors
2. `tsc --noEmit` — TypeScript must compile with zero errors
3. `npm test` — all unit tests must pass
4. `npm run test:integration` — all integration tests must pass

## No `console.log`
- Use `pino` or `winston` for all logging. `console.log`, `console.error`, `console.warn` are forbidden in production code.
- Logger instance must be imported from a shared module (`src/lib/logger.ts`).

## Async/Await Everywhere
- No raw Promise chains (`.then/.catch`). No callbacks.
- Every async function must have an explicit `Promise<T>` return type.
- Use `async/await` for all I/O operations including database calls, HTTP requests, and file operations.
